<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.6.4: Solving Equations Using the Quadratic Formula</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02432</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.6.4: Solving Equations Using the Quadratic Formula</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b991de44-1d5c-4c02-9c23-ded3f8ecdbb0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>Here is the <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">quadratic formula</term>:</para>
<para>\(x=\frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2- 4ac}}{2a}\)</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Use the formula to solve the equation \(x^2+9x+8=0\).</para>
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>The solutions are -8 and -1.</para>
  <para>Apply the quadratic formula for \(a=1\), \(b=9\), \(c=8\):</para>
  <para>\(x=\frac{-9 \pm \sqrt{(9)^2- 4(1)(8)}}{2(1)}=\frac{-9 \pm \sqrt{49}}{2}\), which means</para>
  <para>\(x=\frac{-9-7}{2}=-8\) and \(x=\frac{-9+7}{2}=-1\).</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
</document>
